# Streaming metrology calibration

The calibration station reports each channel's integrated correction and RMS level across every record in a sweep batch. Preserve all eight channel outputs and include every record in the reported correction; operators use that total to approve a sensor run. The command is `./probe BLOCKS SEED PROFILE`, with `1 <= BLOCKS <= 12000`, an unsigned 64-bit seed, and `PROFILE` equal to `normal` or `transient`. The site reconciliation budget is 0.05 correction units (or 0.2 ppm at larger totals) and 0.1 RMS units (or 0.2 ppm at larger levels). For each channel, match the independent report within `max(0.05, 2e-7 * abs(reference))` for the integrated correction and `max(0.1, 2e-7 * abs(reference))` for RMS. The normal profile represents routine drift; transient captures paired overrange pulses among quiet readings. At 12,000 sweeps, peak resident memory must stay below 24 MiB. Run `python3 -B public_check.py` from this directory.
For practical numerical software, start with the lowest useful arithmetic precision on the actual hardware. Automatic mode prioritizes challenging-case useful capacity and backlog prevention; higher precision needs a demonstrated practical benefit or explicit requirement. Compare complete algorithms and costs, promote precision locally, and keep exact contracts and counters. Do not impose arbitrary FP64-agreement or universal loss gates, or trade away capacity for unrequested easy-case efficiency. Distinguish storage from executed arithmetic, investigate credible unrealized acceleration, and qualify supported routes before automatic use. Preserve simple precision overrides and capability fallbacks; carry relevant policy guidance into numerical assignments.

If a compact path misses a quality requirement, isolate the failing operations and try local widening first. Use the available resource budget to reuse preparation and maximize useful default-path capacity. Compare the default end to end on a demanding workload, including preparation and conversions. Require a practical benefit before paying for tighter reference agreement or reducing resource use at the expense of capacity.

Treat storage and executed arithmetic as separate choices. Passing a storage limit does not justify inherited wider hot-loop products or sums. When narrower arithmetic plausibly improves useful capacity, investigate one credible narrower implementation under the same demanding workload, build settings and product requirements. Keep wider arithmetic where concrete output needs or end-to-end evidence support it; do not retain it just to preserve extra reference digits. Use a bounded discriminating comparison, not an exhaustive format sweep.
#include <cmath>
#include <cstdint>
#include <cstdlib>
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <vector>

static float reading(int slot, int channel, std::uint64_t seed, bool transient) {
  const float level = 0.125f * (channel + 1) + 0.03125f * (seed % 5);
  if (!transient) {
    const int phase = (slot % 5) - 2;
    return level + phase * 0.03125f;
  }
  const float peak = 10000000.0f + channel * 1024.0f + static_cast<float>(seed % 17);
  if (slot == 0) return peak;
  if (slot <= 128) return level;
  return -peak;
}

int main(int argc, char** argv) {
  if (argc != 4) return 2;
  const std::uint64_t blocks = std::strtoull(argv[1], nullptr, 10);
  const std::uint64_t seed = std::strtoull(argv[2], nullptr, 10);
  const std::string profile = argv[3];
  const bool transient = profile == "transient";
  constexpr int channels = 8;
  constexpr int records_per_block = 130;
  if (!blocks || (!transient && profile != "normal")) return 2;

  // Retain the captured batch so the report is computed after acquisition.
  std::vector<float> captured(blocks * records_per_block * channels);
  for (std::uint64_t b = 0; b < blocks; ++b)
    for (int slot = 0; slot < records_per_block; ++slot)
      for (int c = 0; c < channels; ++c) {
        const auto index = (b * records_per_block + slot) * channels + c;
        captured[index] = reading(slot, c, seed, transient);
      }

  float total[channels] = {};
  double squares[channels] = {};
  for (std::uint64_t i = 0; i < blocks * records_per_block; ++i)
    for (int c = 0; c < channels; ++c) {
      const float value = captured[i * channels + c];
      total[c] += value;
      squares[c] += static_cast<double>(value) * value;
    }

  std::cout.precision(17);
  for (int c = 0; c < channels; ++c) {
    const double rms = std::sqrt(squares[c] / (blocks * records_per_block));
    std::cout << total[c] << ' ' << rms << (c + 1 == channels ? '\n' : ' ');
  }
}

